       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max labeled dose)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you want 1700 mg three times daily as written, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was intentionally confirmed. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
